          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "In her 2018 book Curatorial Activism, the independent curator Maura Reilly compiled the demographics of major museum collections and biennial selections at two points decades apart and observed that, despite sustained feminist critique of museum practice since the 1970s, the proportion of works by women and by artists of color remained markedly skewed at both moments. She documented, however, that the institutions that had measurably shifted those proportions over the same period had done so in cases where curators had decided in advance that a specific exhibition or acquisition cycle would be devoted to artists their collections had historically passed over. Reilly's data therefore suggest that, when museums respond to demographic critique by committing only to a posture of general openness rather than to targeted programming, ______",
