          "skill": "words-in-context",
          "passage": "Looking back on the early years of the Green Belt Movement in her 2006 memoir, the Kenyan ecologist Wangari Maathai described how she came to see tree planting as more than a symbolic gesture. On hillsides where decades of cash-crop agriculture had stripped the topsoil and dried up seasonal streams, the indigenous trees her groups planted ______ a watershed function the cleared land had lost: their root systems held soil in place during heavy rains, and the resulting cover allowed groundwater to recharge rather than run off.",
