          "passage": "Building on her earlier work at hydrothermal vents, the microbial ecologist Colleen Cavanaugh has more recently turned to the deep-sea mussels that crowd around cold methane seeps on the continental margins. In a 2006 review, she and her co-authors describe how the mussels' gill tissue houses dense colonies of methane-oxidizing bacteria that extract energy from seep methane and pass organic carbon to the host. The arrangement, the authors argue, ______ the mussels in environments where photosynthetic food chains never reach: nourishment is supplied internally, by the symbiont, rather than imported from above.",
